title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1932 and inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/weimar_coalition_2.jpg
max-visits: 12
# subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Germany.

= Inter-Party Relationships

[? if uspd_formed = 0 and burgfrieden = 0 : The <span style="color: var(--spd_color)">SPD</span> cannot govern by itself yet. Because we do not have an electoral majority, we need the support of other parties. We are currently in a political pact with all the other parties. ?]
[? if uspd_formed = 1 and kpd_formed = 0 : The <span style="color: var(--uspd_color)">USPD</span> cannot govern alone, yet. As a splinter of a major party we need the support of the major parties. We could build connections with the other parties. ?]
[? if kpd_formed = 1 : The <span style="color: var(--kpd_color)">KPD</span> cannot govern alone, yet. As a splinter party of a splinter party we could use the support of the major parties. Perhaps we should build connections with the other parties. ?]

- @liberals: Strengthen our bonds with the left-liberal [+ ddp_name +] and conservative-liberal [+ dvp_name +].
- @center: Strengthen our bonds with the Catholic Center Party.
- @socdems: Work towards repairing relationships with the Social Democratic Party.
- @kpd_alone: The SPD can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@socdems
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
view-if: uspd_formed = 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: {!
	Q.resources -= 1
	Q.kpd_inter_party_seen += 1
!}
go-to: spd_1 if spd_relation <= 40; spd_rectification_of_history if spd_relation >= 40 and spd_rectified_history = 0 and spartacist_uprising = 1; spd_2 if spd_coalition_success = 1 and spd_rectified_history = 1

@spd_1
on-arrival: spd_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); left_dissent += 2; z_relation -= 2; dvp_relation -= 3

The social democrats are suspicious of our overtures, as they consider us too radical. However, connections are made at the grassroots and local levels.

@spd_rectification_of_history

One stumbling block for our relations with the <span style="color: var(--spd_color)">SPD</span> is our history of conflict, dating back to 1918 and 1919. The <span style="color: var(--spd_color)">SPD</span> has refused to denounce Gustav Noske, the <span style="color: var(--spd_color)">SPD</span> "bloodhound" who ordered the violent suppression of the Spartacist uprising and other <span style="color: var(--kpd_color)">KPD</span> revolts. They are also to blame for the deaths of Rosa Luxemburg and Karl Liebknecht, two <span style="color: var(--spd_color)">SPD</span>-turned-<span style="color: var(--kpd_color)">KPD</span> leaders who were killed during the suppression of the uprising.

For further improvements in SPD relations, it will be necessary to demand the SPD expel Noske, and hold some sort of commemoration for Luxemburg and Liebknecht.

- @yes_history: Yes, we must demand they apologize for their past actions.
- @no_history: No, we will not collaborate with these traitors.

@yes_history
on-arrival: left_dissent += 8; left_strength -= 2; neorevisionist_dissent += 5; reform_dissent -= 6; reformist_strength += 5; spd_rectified_history = 1; z_relation -= 6; dvp_relation -= 6; ddp_relation -= 4; spd_relation += 8*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 1

As part of normalizing relations with the SPD, we have demanded they acknowledge the wrongdoings of their past. They have expelled Noske, and have held public commemorations for those killed by troops during the uprisings.

[?if ebert_dead = 0 : They have even expelled Friedrich Ebert.?]
[?if ebert_dead = 1 : They have even denounced Friedrich Ebert.?]

This leads to tensions with the center and leftists within our party, and criticism from the conservative and liberal parties.

@no_history
on-arrival: spd_relation -= 3; left_dissent -= 3;

We have no need to collaborate with these traitors to the revolution. 

@spd_2
on-arrival: kpd_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if kpd_inter_party_seen <= 1; left_dissent += 2; z_relation -= 3; dvp_relation -= 3

After the success of the coalition government with the SPD, they are much more amenable to us.


@center
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: {!
	Q.resources -= 1
	if (Q.z_party_leader == "Joos") {Q.z_relation += 2}
!}
go-to: center_op if z_in_government = 1 and kpd_in_government = 0 and chancellor != "Brüning"; center_coalition if kpd_in_government = 1 and z_in_government = 1; center_bruning if chancellor = "Brüning"; center_burger if burgfrieden = 1 and uspd_formed = 0; center_burger_2 if burgfrieden = 1 and uspd_formed = 1

@center_op
on-arrival: z_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We are currently in opposition to the Center-led government, but that does not preclude the general building of feelings of good will.

@center_coalition
on-arrival: z_relation += 8*(1 - dissent)

We are currently coalition partners with them, so improving relations comes naturally.

@center_bruning
on-arrival: z_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

The Brüning semi-autocratic regime makes building friendly relations difficult, but not impossible.

@center_burger
on-arrival: z_relation += 5*(1 - dissent)

We are currently in the Burgfrieden truce with the other parties, so improving relations is easy.

@center_burger_2
on-arrival: z_relation += 3*(1 - dissent)

We are currently outside the Burgfrieden truce with the other parties, so improving relations more difficult.


@liberals
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: {!
	Q.resources -= 1
	Q.ddp_relation += 3*(1 - Q.dissent) 
!}

The [+ ddp_name +] and [+ dvp_name +] are our natural enemies, improving relations will be difficult. Nevertheless, we will try to sway them.


@kpd_alone

Whether it is because we *cannot* or *will not*, we do not make ties with other parties at this moment.

- @return: Continue...
